        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "A is \\(50\\%\\) more efficient than B. Working together, they complete a job in \\(12\\) days. In how many days can B alone complete the job?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Let B's daily work rate be \\(r\\). A's rate is \\(1.5r\\), and \\(2.5r=\\frac{1}{12}\\). Thus \\(r=\\frac{1}{30}\\), which would suggest \\(30\\) days. However, the stated efficiency relation means A completes \\(50\\%\\) more work than B, so the correct calculation is \\(\\frac{1}{T_A}=\\frac{3}{2}\\frac{1}{T_B}\\), with \\(\\frac{1}{T_A}+\\frac{1}{T_B}=\\frac{1}{12}\\), giving \\(T_B=30\\) days.",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
