        "question_title": "A pedestrian and a cyclist leave point \\(A\\) for point \\(B\\) simultaneously. The cyclist reaches \\(B\\), turns back, and meets the pedestrian \\(1\\,\\mathrm{h}\\) after the start. If the pedestrian reaches \\(B\\) \\(3\\,\\mathrm{h}\\) after the start, what is the ratio of the cyclist's speed to the pedestrian's speed?",
