        "explanation": "Let \\(AB=D\\). The pedestrian's speed is \\(\\frac{D}{3}\\). If the cyclist's speed is \\(v\\), then after \\(1\\,\\mathrm{h}\\) the cyclist's position is \\(2D-v\\), because the cyclist has travelled to \\(B\\) and returned. At the meeting, \\(2D-v=\\frac{D}{3}\\), so \\(v=\\frac{5D}{3}\\). Therefore, the speed ratio is \\(\\frac{5D}{3}:\\frac{D}{3}=5:1\\).",
